          "page": 1,
          "paragraph_id": "fictional-alpha-p0002",
          "start": 0,
          "text": "Experiment A uses material Aerogel A for pollutant methylene blue. The budget is initial concentration 40 mg/L, adsorbent dose 1 g/L, contact time 120 min, temperature 298 K."
        },
        {
          "content_sha256": "9dd6e0d37220e4c1089ce4f07c8b605c5d95ce269a74048c0849dc499b48f9c5",
          "end": 137,
          "page": 1,
          "paragraph_id": "fictional-alpha-p0003",
          "start": 0,
          "text": "Metric definition: adsorption_capacity means the retained pollutant mass divided by dry adsorbent mass, expressed in mg/g at equilibrium."
        },
        {
          "content_sha256": "7735dd86e0923dbcb7af4fe4dcf9cace9a7bf5c48f340e689f8f2d6fa525844c",
          "end": 62,
          "page": 1,
          "paragraph_id": "fictional-alpha-p0004",
          "start": 0,
          "text": "For Experiment A, the adsorption_capacity result was 128 mg/g."
        },
        {
          "content_sha256": "a264f1469059c51ed9205e6c0c27438bafef8e24081578c5cc0bb18b8a7ec2ae",
          "end": 149,
          "page": 1,
          "paragraph_id": "fictional-alpha-p0005",
          "start": 0,
          "text": "A later author note for Experiment A revised adsorption_capacity to 132 mg/g using the same reported conditions; the note did not explain the change."
        }
      ],
